            <div xml:id="d48-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0346" n="132" xml:id="pg132"/>

                <head>No. 3.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Li. Guardian General of Fu-Ping Fu to
                        Mr. Drew,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">June 7 th.</hi></p>
                <p>A communication in reply. On receipt of your dispatch in answer to my former one,
                    I read its contents carefully.</p>
                <p>I have control of local matters only, and dare not take on myself to discuss any
                    matters belonging to the central government; I have accordingly transmitted your
                    reply to my superior officer, the minister, who is general and governor of
                    Kang-Hoa prefecture; and have to-day heard that a dispatch from him has just
                    been sent on board your honorable vessel.</p>
                <p>I trust that all future correspondence will be carried on with the official above
                    named, as I cannot presume to interfere in it further.</p>
                <p>A necessary communication in reply to Mr. Drew, acting secretary of legation.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tung-Chih</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian chinese-era chinese-lunisolar" when="1871-06-07"
                                >10<hi rendition="#italic">th year</hi>, 4<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                moon</hi>, 20<hi rendition="#italic">th day</hi>, (June 7,
                            1871.</date>)</dateline></closer>
            </div>
